# Keep the working tree LF on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true, which checks files out as CRLF. The Node
# tooling here (vitest rewriting snapshots, in particular) writes LF, so on Windows the tree
# would drift back to LF and git would then report those files as permanently modified —
# `git status` dirty with an empty `git diff`. That is confusing on its own, and it makes
# `npm run update` refuse to run, since it declines to pull over local edits.
#
# Every blob in this repo is already stored LF, so this changes no committed content; it only
# stops the checkout from converting to CRLF. text=auto still leaves real binaries alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
